Subject: [PATCH] Handle ARM64 cache maintenance on read-only memory slots

DAX executable mappings in recent kernels issue IC IVAU on the PMEM store.
ARM reports this as a write-like NISV fault. Opt into NISV exits only for VMs registering read-only memory and skip
only cache-maintenance operations inside registered read-only slots, keeping
actual stores and unrelated faults as guest external aborts. Synchronize slot tracking with
KVM registration and removal so vCPUs cannot observe stale permissions.

diff --git a/hypervisor/src/kvm/aarch64.rs b/hypervisor/src/kvm/aarch64.rs
index 272328978..04f6bc90b 100644
--- a/hypervisor/src/kvm/aarch64.rs
+++ b/hypervisor/src/kvm/aarch64.rs
@@ -281,7 +281,70 @@ impl VmAArch64 for KvmVm {
